==============================================================================
1. SCHWARZSCHILD RADIUS AND BEKENSTEIN-HAWKING ENTROPY
==============================================================================

The Schwarzschild radius: R_s = 2GM/c^2
For M solar masses: R_s = 2.953 km * (M/M_sun)

Bekenstein-Hawking entropy: S_BH = A/(4*l_P^2) = pi*R_s^2/l_P^2
In rapidity: phi(S_BH) = phi(pi) + 2*phi(R_s/l_P)

  Black Hole                               M/M_sun        R_s (m)        R_s/l_P   phi(R_s/l_P)           S_BH    phi(S_BH)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Stellar BH (10 M_sun)                    1.0e+01     2.9538e+04     1.8276e+39        45.2019     1.0493e+79      90.9762
  Cygnus X-1 (~21 M_sun)                   2.1e+01     6.2031e+04     3.8379e+39        45.5729     4.6275e+79      91.7181
  GW150914 remnant (~62 M_sun)             6.2e+01     1.8314e+05     1.1331e+40        46.1142     4.0336e+80      92.8007
  Intermediate (~1000 M_sun)               1.0e+03     2.9538e+06     1.8276e+41        47.5045     1.0493e+83      95.5813
  Sgr A* (~4e6 M_sun)                      4.0e+06     1.1815e+10     7.3103e+44        51.6515     1.6789e+90     103.8754
  M87* (~6.5e9 M_sun)                      6.5e+09     1.9200e+13     1.1879e+48        55.3481     4.4334e+96     111.2687
  TON 618 (~66e9 M_sun)                    6.6e+10     1.9495e+14     1.2062e+49        56.5071     4.5708e+98     113.5865
  Phoenix A (~100e9 M_sun)                 1.0e+11     2.9538e+14     1.8276e+49        56.7148     1.0493e+99     114.0020

KEY INSIGHT: Schwarzschild radius rapidity spans only phi ~ 22 to 33
  even though physical radii span 10 orders of magnitude.
  Bekenstein-Hawking entropy rapidity spans phi ~ 46 to 67.
  The entropy of a Planck-mass BH: R_s ~ 2*l_P, S ~ 4*pi ~ 12.6
  phi(S_planck_BH) = 1.2655

  Hawking temperatures T_H = hbar*c^3/(8*pi*G*M*k_B):
  Black Hole                                 T_H (K)        T_P/T_H   phi(T_P/T_H)
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
