4. RUNNING COUPLING CONSTANTS --> GRAND UNIFICATION IN RAPIDITY
==============================================================================

  Coupling constants at M_Z = 91.2 GeV:
    alpha_s  = 0.1180       1/alpha_s  = 8.47     phi(1/alpha_s)  = 1.0685
    alpha_W  = 0.0338       1/alpha_W  = 29.60     phi(1/alpha_W)  = 1.6939
    alpha_EM = 0.007819     1/alpha_EM = 127.90    phi(1/alpha_EM) = 2.4256

  At GUT scale ~10^16 GeV:
    alpha_GUT ~ 0.0400      1/alpha_GUT = 25.0      phi(1/alpha_GUT) = 1.6094

  Rapidity SPREAD at M_Z:
    phi(1/alpha_EM) - phi(1/alpha_s) = 1.3571
    phi(1/alpha_W)  - phi(1/alpha_s) = 0.6254

  Rapidity of the energy scales:
    M_Z  = 91.2 GeV:  phi(M_Z/m_e)  = 6.0461
    GUT  = 10^16 GeV: phi(GUT/m_e)  = 22.2103
    Planck = 1.22e19 GeV: phi(M_Pl/m_e) = 25.7636

  UNIFICATION in rapidity: the three inverse couplings converge from a
  rapidity spread of 1.36 at M_Z to ~0 at the GUT scale.
  The energy range from M_Z to GUT in rapidity:
    phi(E_GUT/E_Z) = 16.1642

  One-loop running of 1/alpha_i vs ln(mu/M_Z):
    ln(mu/M_Z)  phi(mu/M_Z)  1/alpha_1  1/alpha_2  1/alpha_3     spread
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
           0.0         0.00      59.00      29.60       8.47      50.53
           5.0         2.50      55.74      32.12      14.04      41.69
          10.0         5.00      52.47      34.64      19.62      32.86
          15.0         7.50      49.21      37.16      25.19      24.03
          20.0        10.00      45.95      39.68      30.76      15.19
          25.0        12.50      42.69      42.20      36.33       6.36
          30.0        15.00      39.42      44.72      41.90       5.30
          33.0        16.50      37.47      46.23      45.24       8.77

  Note: ln(mu/M_Z) IS 2*phi(mu/M_Z) -- the running is LINEAR in rapidity!
  Unification means the three lines converge to a single point in rapidity space.
  The GUT scale at ln(mu/M_Z) ~ 33 corresponds to phi(mu/M_Z) ~ 16.5.


