==============================================================================
6. CMB TEMPERATURE AND AGE OF THE UNIVERSE
==============================================================================

  CMB temperature: T_CMB = 2.7255 K
  Planck temperature: T_P = 1.4168e+32 K
  Ratio T_P / T_CMB = 5.1983e+31

  phi(T_P / T_CMB) = 36.5142

  This is the "rapidity distance" from the CMB to the Planck temperature.
  Equivalently, the universe has cooled by rapidity 36.5 from Planck epoch.

  Age of universe: 4.3549e+17 seconds
  In Planck times: 8.0778e+60
  phi(age / t_P)  = 70.1221

  REMARKABLE: The rapidity of the age (in Planck times) ~ 70.1
  and the rapidity of the temperature ratio ~ 36.5
  are of the SAME ORDER. Both measure "how far we are from the Planck epoch."

  Their difference: 33.6079
  Their ratio: 1.9204

  In a radiation-dominated universe, T ~ 1/sqrt(t), so:
    T_P/T_CMB ~ sqrt(age/t_P) => phi(T_P/T_CMB) ~ phi(age/t_P)/2
    Expected: 35.0611  vs  Actual: 36.5142
    (Differs because universe is NOT radiation-dominated for most of its history)


